<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech 1996 retail sales +9.6 pct (+3.6 pct 95).</title>
<headline>Czech 1996 retail sales +9.6 pct (+3.6 pct 95).</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech December retail sales, in real terms, rose 12.5 percent compared with the same month in 1995, putting sales 9.6 percent higher for the whole of 1996 the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The CSU also said that total internal trade rose by 11.2 percent year-on-year in real terms in December.  </p>
<p> CZECH REAL RETAIL SALES	 DEC 96   NOV 96   JAN-DEC 96</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +12.5    +8.3	  +9.6</p>
<p>CZECH REAL INTERNAL TRADE</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +11.2    +9.2	 +11.4</p>
<p>The CSU also gave the following real retail sales data (percentage change year-on-year):</p>
<p>				     DEC 96   NOV 96  JAN-DEC 96</p>
<p>sales, repairs of motor</p>
<p> vehicles plus motor fuel	6.8     12.7     21.8</p>
<p>restaurants and</p>
<p> accommodation		     8.8	8.4	7.2</p>
<p>TRANSPORT</p>
<p>  total			     -1.2     -4.0     10.8</p>
<p>  railways			  +5.1    -11.5	2.7</p>
<p>  road transport		  -0.8     -3.0	7.7</p>
<p>  river			    -25.1    -43.7    -24.8</p>
<p>  air				-17.9    -22.6     -5.6</p>
<p>parallel and support   activities</p>
<p>					14.9     16.6     30.2</p>
<p>Note: All figures are preliminary. Total internal trade includes retail sales plus sales and repairs of motor cars, motor fuel, restaurant services and accommodation.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
